-- chem/algebra.cub — equality of expressions decided by normal form, in place of a grid chosen by hand. A statement
-- about a commutative ring is written once, taking the ring (its addition, its multiplication, the rationals in it)
-- and its variables; at the ring of polynomials in those variables over the rationals its two sides are polynomials,
-- and they are equal as expressions exactly when their difference has every coefficient zero (`al-id`). The same
-- definition at the rationals gives its values. No degree is counted and no points are chosen; the identity holds in
-- every commutative ring containing the rationals. A polynomial is a list of terms (exponents by variable, lowest
-- variable first; coefficient); terms with the same exponents are added when a term is put in.
import "fine.hypercubical"

